{
  "index_test": "in-vitro-only",
  "index_test_evidence": "Human plasma-derived 3D culture (HuP3D) models were created by cross-linking fibrinogen, a blood plasma protein responsible for normal blood clotting when converted into fibrin ( Figure 1 a) [ 33 ], generating a gelatinous-like scaffold matrix using traditional tissue culture surfaces as the recipient mold, with media added on top to overcome drying of the matrix ( Figure 1 b).",
  "decision": "exclude",
  "reason": "The study uses in vitro 3D cell cultures derived from human plasma and breast cancer cell lines to predict treatment responses. It does not involve whole, live non-human animals as the index test. While it mentions animal models in the introduction as a comparison, the primary methodology and predictive model described are in vitro."
}
